ons><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1054022A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUDA FUMIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUDA, FUMIO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUDA FUMIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUDA, FUMIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A catalyst which comprises a compound of a transition metal in Groups 8 to 10 of the Periodic Table having a nitrogenous tridentate ligand and an organoaluminum compound such as trimethylaluminum; and a process for producing a polyolefin with the catalyst. The catalyst is highly active and enables a high-molecular polyolefin to be produced. Consequently, a high-molecular polyolefin (especially polyethylene) suitable for practical use can be industrially advantageously produced without using methylaluminoxane, which is expensive, has poor handleability and poor storage stability, and is highly dangerous.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un catalyseur qui comprend un composé d'un métal de transition des groupes 8 à 10 de la table de classification périodique possédant un ligand tridenté azoté, et un composé d'organo-aluminium tel que du triméthylaluminium. Cette invention concerne également un procédé de production d'une polyoléfine à l'aide de ce catalyseur. Ce catalyseur est hautement actif, et permet de produire une polyoléfine qui possède un poids moléculaire élevé. Il est ainsi possible de produire avantageusement et à l'échelle industrielle une polyoléfine qui possède un poids moléculaire élevé et qui convient à un usage pratique, notamment du polyéthylène, ceci sans utiliser de méthylaluminoxane qui est cher, difficilement manipulable, hautement dangereux et possède une stabilité réduite lors de son stockage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>